text:
maria: Quick question — customer support needs a short-term capture of request/response bodies to repro a production bug. Asking for 7 days retention. Can we do this and what exact masking do you want for session tokens and prompt fields?

samir: Are these captures scoped to a single customer/org? who will access the data?

maria: yes single tenant, support + eng will need access. We'll put captures in a temp S3 bucket with limited IAM.

sec-bot: Policy reminder: do not store full auth tokens, credit-card numbers, or raw PII. Prefer one-way pseudonymization (hash/HMAC) for identifiers and redact prompt text that contains PII. See https://intra.redwood/policies/logging-redaction (shortlink).

jess: Short answer: ok with limited scope + timeboxed access. Requirements: mask all bearer/opaque tokens and session IDs in headers and bodies, pseudonymize user identifiers, and DO NOT keep raw full prompts if they may contain PII. Prefer HMAC-with-per-tenant-salt over plain hashing.

alan: For temporary S3, can we auto-expire objects and enable SSE-KMS? I'll set bucket lifecycle and a KMS CMK with access only to support role.

maria: plan: capture only the failing requests, stream to a staging bucket, retain 7d, then auto-delete. Need guidance on token handling in code — do we completely remove header `X-Session` or replace with hash/HMAC?

jess: Replace with HMAC(token || request_id) using tenant-specific salt and store only the HMAC. If you need to correlate across logs, store truncated prompt fingerprint (sha256, keep first 12 chars) + a label; never store full prompt. Example rules: 1) headers: redact value (replace with `REDACTED-HMAC:<hmac>`), 2) body: remove fields named `password`, `ssn`, `credit_card`, 3) prompts: if prompt contains user data, store `PROMPT_REDACTED:<sha256-prefix>` only.

maria: thanks. quick pseudo: 
```
function mask(req) {
  req.headers['X-Session'] = 'REDACTED-HMAC:' + hmac(req.headers['X-Session'], tenant_salt);
  if (req.body.prompt && contains_pii(req.body.prompt)) {
    req.meta.prompt_fingerprint = sha256(req.body.prompt).slice(0,12);
    delete req.body.prompt;
  }
  removeFields(req.body, ['password','ssn','credit_card']);
  return req;
}
```

samir: looks good. who approves the access list for the S3 bucket? need explicit allowlist (support@, eng-oncall@) and justification in ticket.

jess: I'll approve the allowlist once you post the ticket with tenant id and exact S3 path. Make sure to include a timed IAM role (max 7 days) and audit logging turned on.

maria: created ticket #INC-4721 with tenant=acme-inc, s3://temp-debug/acme-inc/2951112223/, retention=7d. tagged @jess for approval.

sec-bot: Audit event: temporary-archive-created -> s3://temp-debug/acme-inc/2951112223/ by maria (expires in 7d).

jess: Approved. Conditions: 1) implement HMAC replacement for X-Session, 2) no raw prompt retention, 3) IAM roles expire automatically, 4) delete objects after 7d, 5) share minimal logs for postmortem. :white_check_mark:

alan: I'll attach lifecycle rule + bucket policy + kms key policy. Ping me when ready and I'll run the delete job after 7d.

maria: implementing now, will post PR with the masking lib and unit tests. tagging for CR: @samir @alan.

samir: will review the PR later today. :thumbsup:

maria: thanks everyone, closing the loop here once PR is merged and infra is in place.
